sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Patient
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant Svc as Booking Service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Patient->>API: POST /api/v1/bookings + Idempotency-Key
    API->>API: Authenticate patient and validate request
    API->>Svc: create_booking(patient, doctor_id, slot_id, reason, key)
    Svc->>DB: BEGIN (request transaction)
    Svc->>DB: Claim/read actor + operation scoped idempotency key

    alt Matching completed key
        DB-->>Svc: Stored booking response
        Svc-->>API: Replay original representation
        API-->>Patient: 200 OK
    else New request
        Svc->>DB: SELECT slot FOR UPDATE
        alt Slot missing, mismatched, unavailable, or already booked
            DB-->>Svc: Conflict/not-found condition
            Svc->>DB: ROLLBACK (including idempotency claim)
            Svc-->>API: Safe error
            API-->>Patient: 404 / 409 error
        else Available future slot owned by doctor
            Svc->>DB: Insert consultation (status = booked)
            Svc->>DB: Update slot status to booked
            Note over DB: Partial unique index prevents a second active consultation
            Svc->>DB: Store completed idempotency response
            Svc->>DB: Insert minimal booking.created outbox event
            Svc->>DB: COMMIT
            DB-->>Svc: Commit successful
            Svc-->>API: Created booking
            API-->>Patient: 201 Created
        end
    end

    Note over Svc,DB: No network call or event dispatch occurs while the slot lock is held.
